    <innerclass refid="class_m2_1_1_reader" prot="public">M2::Reader</innerclass>
    <innernamespace refid="namespace_m2">M2</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="class_m2_1_1_reader" kindref="compound">M2::Reader</ref>&lt;RingType&gt;</computeroutput> <mdash/> parse a single ring element from a <computeroutput>std::istream</computeroutput>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Declares the per-ring stream reader: construct with a <computeroutput>RingType&amp;</computeroutput> and call <computeroutput>read(istream, result)</computeroutput> to consume one element&apos;s textual form and land its value in <computeroutput>RingType::ElementType</computeroutput>. The header forward-declares the primary template and provides the explicit specialisation for <computeroutput>ARingZZp</computeroutput>; per-ring <computeroutput>.cpp</computeroutput> specialisations parse to a temporary (<computeroutput>mpz_t</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>mpfr_t</computeroutput>, ...) using the underlying library&apos;s stream operator and then call the ring&apos;s <computeroutput>set_from_*</computeroutput> to land the value in <computeroutput>ElementType</computeroutput>.</para>
<para>The pattern keeps parse logic close to each ring&apos;s native value type instead of going through a single <computeroutput>Ring::from_text</computeroutput> virtual. Used by matrix / polynomial I/O, the streaming polynomial parsers, and test harnesses that read serialised inputs.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="aring-zzp_8hpp" kindref="compound">aring-zzp.hpp</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
